From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 12:29:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/43] test(chexc): assumption imports (proposal 5.2.2), 6
 cases

Rewrites the three red placeholder cases onto the suite's established
multi-package pattern (DEPENDENCE + %compile_lib_opt + %middle, then link the
staticlib into the consumer), matching API/std/reflect/isSubtypeOf_test_cjnative.
The previous form used an import shape whose validity I could not confirm and a
non-standard two-package invocation.

Cases:
- assume_basic          functions, methods and constructors all covered
- assume_bare           '@AssumeThrows' with no list assumes 'Exception'
- assume_alias_and_inference   a capability list alias (6.1) in the annotation,
                        and an assumed requirement inferred (6.3) into a
                        clause-free internal declaration's list
- assume_neg            an unhandled assumed requirement is a missing capability
- assume_misplaced_neg  the annotation is rejected off an 'import'
- assume_other_package  the assumption does not reach calls into other packages

legacy_db.cj is the unchecked dependency, compiled without the flag so it
declares no clauses -- which is the situation the feature exists for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
